<p>The <em>Enquiry</em> is more reader-friendly than the <em>Meditations</em>, but Hume’s core arguments can feel slippery on a first pass because he is asking you to question things that seem obvious. This video introduces empiricism, the problem of induction, and Hume’s analysis of causation before you encounter them in the text.</p>
